BSP-Yocto-EdgeAI-AM68x-v0.2                    2025-12-17
==================================================================

- Based on BSP-Yocto-Ampliphy-AM68x-PD24.1.0 and TI SDK-LINUX-AM68A 9.2
- Update poky (Yocto 4.0.31+) and meta-openembedded to recent
- Linux TI vendor kernel v6.1.80 (based on TI tag 09.02.00.009)
- U-Boot TI v2023.04 (based on TI tag 09.02.00.009)
- Yocto Kirkstone
- meta-edgeai-phytec (tag 09.02.01.00-phy2)

Tested Yocto images:
--------------------

- ampliphy-xwayland/phytec-edgeai-image:
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-2
  * phyboard-izar-am68x-3


Build environment:
------------------

- Ubuntu 22.04 64-bit

Features:
---------

- Add fdplink-3 pipeline examples to use PHYTEC phycam-L, including DT overlays.
- Patch edgeai-tiovx-apps to have PHYTEC phycam support and add an example config.
- Add extension script to setup environment variable in SDK with common environment 
  setup script to compile TI EdgeAI examples with nearly no changes (see Known issues).
- Due to issues with git tags in TI repositories and PHYTEC's use of repo-tool for
  metalayer setup, switch ti-vision-apps to use git fetcher (so URLs and revisions
  in receipe) instead of TI manifest.

Known Issues
------------

- SDK: 'make' is not part of the SDK. Therefore, set
  'CMAKE_FIND_ROOT_PATH_MODE_PROGRAM' to 'BOTH' in i.e.
  https://github.com/TexasInstruments/edgeai-tiovx-apps/blob/develop/cmake/cross_compile_aarch64.cmake
  to cross-compile example.
- There may be build issues due to sstate caching during fetch for npm packages
  cors and express. Build without cahce or clean icu package sstates.
